-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, sections 101 and 104 to 107 (piece dg1):
-- who may incorporate and for what purposes; what "certificate of incorporation" includes; the certificate
-- as evidence; when corporate existence begins; what the incorporators may do. Layer 1: nobody's point of view.
-- Section 102 (contents of the certificate) is in dg1-s102a-required-contents.l4, dg1-s102b-optional-provisions.l4 and
-- dg1-s102e-name-reservation.l4, section 103 (execution, filing and effect) in dg1-s103-filing.l4, which this module calls.
--
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering of the Delaware Code Online, not the
-- official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N; an ellipsis means the line goes on.

§ `Section 101 -- Incorporators; how corporation formed; purposes`

-- "Any person, partnership, association or corporation": the text does not define "person" for this section
-- (section 203(c)(6) defines it for section 203 only), so a natural person, the four kinds of partnership, a
-- corporation of any kind, and the three kinds of association the core lists are covered. A limited liability
-- company, statutory trust, real estate investment trust or common-law trust is named by neither word, and the
-- answer for those is NOTHING (not covered). Residence, domicile and state of incorporation are disregarded, so
-- no rule here reads where an entity was formed.
-- src:35 | (a) Any person, partnership, association or corporation, singly or jointly with others, and without regard to such person’s or entity’s residence, domicile or state of incorporation, may incorporate or organize a corporation under this chapter by filing with the Division of Corporations in the Department of State a certificate of incorporation which shall be executed, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 101(a) (src:35)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 101(a) the entity may incorporate or organize a corporation under this chapter` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a natural person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation` its THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a general partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a limited partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability limited partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a joint-stock association` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a business trust or association` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any other unincorporated business or association` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability company` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a statutory trust` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a real estate investment trust` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a common-law trust` THEN NOTHING

-- The corporation is incorporated by filing a certificate of incorporation, executed, acknowledged and filed in
-- accordance with section 103 (all called here from dg1-s103-filing.l4).
-- src:35 | (a) Any person, partnership, association or corporation, singly or jointly with others, and without regard to such person’s or entity’s residence, domicile or state of incorporation, may incorporate or organize a corporation under this chapter by filing with the Division of Corporations in the Department of State a certificate of incorporation which shall be executed, …
-- src:35 | acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 101(a) (src:35)
GIVEN i IS A `s 103(a) Instrument`
      incorporators IS A `s 103(a)(1) Signing by the incorporators`
      corporation IS A `s 103(a)(2) Signing for the corporation`
      acknowledgment IS A `s 103(b) Acknowledgment`
      steps IS A `s 103(c) Steps of filing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 101(a) the corporation has been incorporated by filing the certificate of incorporation` i incorporators corporation acknowledgment steps MEANS
        i's `the instrument is the certificate of incorporation`
    AND `s 103(a) the instrument is executed as required` i incorporators corporation
    AND `s 103(b) the requirement that the instrument be acknowledged is satisfied` acknowledgment
    AND `s 103(c) the instrument has been filed` steps

-- Any lawful business or purposes, except as the Constitution or other law of this State may otherwise provide.
-- src:36 | (b) A corporation may be incorporated or organized under this chapter to conduct or promote any lawful business or purposes, except as may otherwise be provided by the Constitution or other law of this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 101(b) (src:36)
GIVEN `the business or purposes are lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Constitution or other law of this State otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 101(b) a corporation may be incorporated to conduct or promote the business or purposes` `the business or purposes are lawful` `the Constitution or other law of this State otherwise provides` MEANS
        `the business or purposes are lawful`
    AND (NOT (`the Constitution or other law of this State otherwise provides`))

-- Public utilities may be organized under this chapter whether in or outside this State; one that operates
-- within this State is subject also to the special provisions and requirements of Title 26 (not an input here:
-- the outcome of Title 26 is outside this text).
-- src:37 | (c) Corporations for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities, whether in or outside of this State, may be organized under this chapter, but corporations for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities within this State shall be subject to, in addition to this chapter, the special provisions and requirements of Title 26 applicable to such corporations.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 101(c) (src:37)
GIVEN `the corporation is for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 101(c) a corporation for operating public utilities, in or outside this State, may be organized under this chapter` `the corporation is for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities` MEANS
    `the corporation is for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities`

-- src:37 | (c) Corporations for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities, whether in or outside of this State, may be organized under this chapter, but corporations for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities within this State shall be subject to, in addition to this chapter, the special provisions and requirements of Title 26 applicable to such corporations.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 101(c) (src:37)
GIVEN `the corporation is for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public utilities are within this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 101(c) the corporation is subject also to the special provisions and requirements of Title 26` `the corporation is for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities` `the public utilities are within this State` MEANS
        `the corporation is for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities`
    AND `the public utilities are within this State`

§ `Section 104 -- Certificate of incorporation; definition`

-- "Certificate of incorporation", as used in this chapter and unless the context requires otherwise, includes the
-- original certificate and every other instrument, howsoever designated, filed pursuant to any section of this
-- title that has the effect of amending or supplementing it in some respect. The sections the text lists are
-- examples ("or any other section of this title"), so the rule does not test the section number.
-- src:115 | The term “certificate of incorporation,” as used in this chapter, unless the context requires otherwise, includes not only the original certificate of incorporation filed to create a corporation but also all other certificates, agreements of merger or consolidation, plans of reorganization, or other instruments, howsoever designated, which are filed pursuant to § 102, §§ 133-136, § 151, §§ 241-243, § 245, §§ 251-258, §§ 263-264, § 267, § 303, §§ 311-313, or any other section of this title, and which have the effect of amending or supplementing in some respect a corporation’s certificate of incorporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 104 (src:115)
GIVEN `the instrument is the original certificate of incorporation filed to create the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a certificate, agreement of merger or consolidation, plan of reorganization or other instrument, howsoever designated, filed pursuant to a section of this title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument has the effect of amending or supplementing in some respect the corporation's certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context requires otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 104 the instrument is part of the certificate of incorporation` `the instrument is the original certificate of incorporation filed to create the corporation` `the instrument is a certificate, agreement of merger or consolidation, plan of reorganization or other instrument, howsoever designated, filed pursuant to a section of this title` `the instrument has the effect of amending or supplementing in some respect the corporation's certificate of incorporation` `the context requires otherwise` MEANS
        (NOT (`the context requires otherwise`))
    AND (   `the instrument is the original certificate of incorporation filed to create the corporation`
         OR (    `the instrument is a certificate, agreement of merger or consolidation, plan of reorganization or other instrument, howsoever designated, filed pursuant to a section of this title`
             AND `the instrument has the effect of amending or supplementing in some respect the corporation's certificate of incorporation`))

§ `Section 105 -- Certificate of incorporation and other certificates; evidence`

-- src:119 | A copy of a certificate of incorporation, or a restated certificate of incorporation, or of any other certificate which has been filed in the office of the Secretary of State as required by any provision of this title shall, when duly certified by the Secretary of State, be received in all courts, public offices and official bodies as prima facie evidence of:
-- src:120 | (1) Due execution, acknowledgment and filing of the instrument;
-- src:121 | (2) Observance and performance of all acts and conditions necessary to have been observed and performed precedent to the instrument becoming effective; and
-- src:122 | (3) Any other facts required or permitted by law to be stated in the instrument.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 105 (src:119-122)
DECLARE `s 105 Matter evidenced` IS ONE OF
    `due execution, acknowledgment and filing of the instrument`
    `observance and performance of all acts and conditions necessary to have been observed and performed precedent to the instrument becoming effective`
    `any other fact required or permitted by law to be stated in the instrument`
    `a matter that is not a fact of those kinds`

-- A copy of a certificate of incorporation (or restated certificate, or any other certificate filed as this title
-- requires), duly certified by the Secretary of State, is received in all courts, public offices and official
-- bodies as prima facie evidence of the three kinds of matter. Without a certified copy, or for another matter,
-- the section does not speak (NOTHING).
-- src:119 | A copy of a certificate of incorporation, or a restated certificate of incorporation, or of any other certificate which has been filed in the office of the Secretary of State as required by any provision of this title shall, when duly certified by the Secretary of State, be received in all courts, public offices and official bodies as prima facie evidence of:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 105 (src:119-122)
GIVEN `the copy has been duly certified by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument was filed in the office of the Secretary of State as required by a provision of this title` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 105 Matter evidenced`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 the certified copy is received as prima facie evidence of the matter` `the copy has been duly certified by the Secretary of State` `the instrument was filed in the office of the Secretary of State as required by a provision of this title` matter MEANS
    IF `the copy has been duly certified by the Secretary of State` AND `the instrument was filed in the office of the Secretary of State as required by a provision of this title`
    THEN CONSIDER matter
         WHEN `due execution, acknowledgment and filing of the instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `observance and performance of all acts and conditions necessary to have been observed and performed precedent to the instrument becoming effective` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `any other fact required or permitted by law to be stated in the instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a matter that is not a fact of those kinds` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 106 -- Commencement of corporate existence`

-- Upon the filing of the certificate of incorporation, executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103,
-- the incorporators who signed it, and their successors and assigns, are from the date of filing a body corporate
-- by the name in the certificate, "subject to § 103(d)": an effective date specified in the certificate under
-- section 103(d) postpones the existence to that date. The result is NOTHING if the certificate was not
-- executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103 (the section does not apply).
-- src:126 | Upon the filing with the Secretary of State of the certificate of incorporation, executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title, the incorporator or incorporators who signed the certificate, and such incorporator’s or incorporators’ successors and assigns, shall, from the date of such filing, be and constitute a body corporate, by the name set forth in the certificate, subject to § 103(d) of this title and subject to dissolution or other termination of its existence as provided in this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 106 (src:126)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation was executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the certificate of incorporation was filed` IS A DATE
      `the later effective date the certificate specifies` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 106 the date from which the incorporators are a body corporate` `the certificate of incorporation was executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103` `the date on which the certificate of incorporation was filed` `the later effective date the certificate specifies` MEANS
    IF `the certificate of incorporation was executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103`
    THEN `s 103(d) the date on which the instrument is effective` `the date on which the certificate of incorporation was filed` `the later effective date the certificate specifies`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The body corporate bears the name set forth in the certificate, and is subject to dissolution or other
-- termination of its existence as provided in this chapter.
-- src:126 | Upon the filing with the Secretary of State of the certificate of incorporation, executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title, the incorporator or incorporators who signed the certificate, and such incorporator’s or incorporators’ successors and assigns, shall, from the date of such filing, be and constitute a body corporate, by the name set forth in the certificate, subject to § 103(d) of this title and subject to dissolution or other termination of its existence as provided in this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 106 (src:126)
GIVEN `the name set forth in the certificate of incorporation` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 106 the name by which the body corporate exists` `the name set forth in the certificate of incorporation` MEANS
    `the name set forth in the certificate of incorporation`

-- src:126 | Upon the filing with the Secretary of State of the certificate of incorporation, executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title, the incorporator or incorporators who signed the certificate, and such incorporator’s or incorporators’ successors and assigns, shall, from the date of such filing, be and constitute a body corporate, by the name set forth in the certificate, subject to § 103(d) of this title and subject to dissolution or other termination of its existence as provided in this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 106 (src:126)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the date from which the incorporators are a body corporate` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the corporation has been dissolved or its existence otherwise terminated as provided in this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 106 the body corporate exists on the day` `the day in question` `the date from which the incorporators are a body corporate` `the corporation has been dissolved or its existence otherwise terminated as provided in this chapter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date from which the incorporators are a body corporate`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST began THEN
            (`the day in question` AT LEAST began)
        AND (NOT (`the corporation has been dissolved or its existence otherwise terminated as provided in this chapter`))

§ `Section 107 -- Powers of incorporators`

-- src:130 | If the persons who are to serve as directors until the first annual meeting of stockholders have not been named in the certificate of incorporation, the incorporator or incorporators, until the directors are elected, shall manage the affairs of the corporation and may do whatever is necessary and proper to …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 107 (src:130)
DECLARE `s 107 Act of the incorporators` IS ONE OF
    `adopting the original bylaws of the corporation`
    `electing directors while the incorporators manage the corporation`
    `another act necessary and proper to perfect the organization of the corporation`
    `an act that is not necessary and proper to perfect the organization of the corporation`

-- If the persons who are to serve as directors until the first annual meeting have not been named in the
-- certificate, the incorporators, until the directors are elected, manage the affairs of the corporation.
-- src:130 | If the persons who are to serve as directors until the first annual meeting of stockholders have not been named in the certificate of incorporation, the incorporator or incorporators, until the directors are elected, shall manage the affairs of the corporation and may do whatever is necessary and proper to perfect the organization of the corporation, including the adoption of the original bylaws of the corporation and the election of directors.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 107 (src:130)
GIVEN `the persons who are to serve as directors until the first annual meeting of stockholders have been named in the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have been elected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 107 the incorporators manage the affairs of the corporation` `the persons who are to serve as directors until the first annual meeting of stockholders have been named in the certificate of incorporation` `the directors have been elected` MEANS
        (NOT (`the persons who are to serve as directors until the first annual meeting of stockholders have been named in the certificate of incorporation`))
    AND (NOT (`the directors have been elected`))

-- While they manage, the incorporators may do whatever is necessary and proper to perfect the organization,
-- including adopting the original bylaws and electing directors. An act that is not necessary and proper is not
-- covered by the section (NOTHING).
-- src:130 | If the persons who are to serve as directors until the first annual meeting of stockholders have not been named in the certificate of incorporation, the incorporator or incorporators, until the directors are elected, shall manage the affairs of the corporation and may do whatever is necessary and proper to perfect the organization of the corporation, including the adoption of the original bylaws of the corporation and the election of directors.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 107 (src:130)
GIVEN `the incorporators manage the affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 107 Act of the incorporators`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107 the incorporators may do the act` `the incorporators manage the affairs of the corporation` act MEANS
    IF `the incorporators manage the affairs of the corporation`
    THEN CONSIDER act
         WHEN `adopting the original bylaws of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `electing directors while the incorporators manage the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `another act necessary and proper to perfect the organization of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an act that is not necessary and proper to perfect the organization of the corporation` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING
